// Runtime-changed BCL members (VERIFICATION-MODEL.md section 3; ADR 0008): calls whose observable
// behaviour changed at the runtime a row's "changedIn" names, even though the call is textually
// identical on both sides. "member" is a prefix matched against CallIdentity.Value
// (Equiv.Core.Matching.ProcedureIdentityNormalizer's "Namespace.Type::Member(ParamType,...)"
// shape), so one row covers every overload of a family, or every member of a type when the
// prefix ends right after "::".
//
// "source" (ADR 0035) says where a row came from: "curated" rows were picked by hand in M2-006,
// "documented" rows come from Microsoft's compatibility pages (M2-007; each is traced to its page
// in docs/runtime-changes-review.md), and "measured" rows carry a witness input (M3-033).
//
// "changedIn" (ADR 0040 decision 2) is the target framework moniker of the first runtime with the new
// behaviour; netcoreapp1.0 marks the .NET Framework to .NET boundary. A row applies to a pair only when
// its changedIn lies in (older runtime, newer runtime]; null means the change point is unknown and the
// row applies whenever the runtimes differ. "coveredFrom" is the oldest .NET version whose changes this
// table lists. Backfilled once by tools/runtime-changes-backfill (P2-054); the measured rows were placed by running
// tools/runtime-diff between adjacent runtimes (P2-113). A member whose behaviour changed at more than one runtime
// has one row per change point.
//
// "precondition" (optional; ticket P2-073) names what a call's arguments must be able to be for the row's change to
// reach it. It reads some of the call's operands, each only when it is a compile-time constant: the row does not apply
// to a call that has at least one of them, all constants, none of which meets the precondition. A call with none of
// them, or with one that is not a constant, gets the row as a row without a precondition does. The values:
//   "caseInsensitivePattern": reads the arguments named pattern and options; met by a pattern with an inline option
//     group that turns i on, such as (?i) or (?i:...), and by options with RegexOptions.IgnoreCase.
//   "twoDigitYearFormat": reads the argument named format; met by a standard (one-character) format and by a custom
//     format with a y or yy specifier.
//   "cultureSensitiveText": reads the receiver and every string argument; met by a string with a character that is
//     not an ASCII letter or digit.
//   "invalidPath": reads every string argument; met by a blank path, one of 248 characters or more, and one with a
//     control character, one of " < > | ? *, or a colon anywhere but after a drive letter.
//
// "ordinalUnaffected" (P2-075), when true, marks a row for a culture-sensitive comparison: a call that passes
// StringComparison.Ordinal or StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase as a constant argument is not flagged by it.
//
// One row is for a call the compiler makes and the source does not write (ADR 0024 as clarified by ticket P2-144):
// the SwitchExpressionException constructor a switch expression calls when no arm matches. Where the reference
// assemblies have no such type the compiler calls InvalidOperationException's, which has no row, so the row flags the
// side that has the type; the bound fingerprint names the constructor on both sides.
//
// x87 vs SSE floating-point on x86 is NOT a row here: floats are an uninterpreted Sort in the
// MVP, so there is no bit-level float semantics yet for a row to flag calls against. Add it once
// floats gain a real encoding (post-MVP).
